{
 "how": "Interaction shares of trained and untrained joins, recomputed from saved weights for Fig. 5c (CPU only).\n\nThe interaction share of a score over the partner pairs (j, k) a join scores is the part of its variance that is not a\nsum f(j) + g(k), divided by its value for independent random scores: (n - 1)^2 / (n^2 - 1) on the full grid (joins\nthat allow j = k, as chess joins beside attention), (n^2 - 3n + 1) / (n^2 - n - 1) on the off-diagonal pairs (SET\njoins and chess joins replacing attention, which score j != k only; additive part fitted by least squares). Sums of\nsquares are taken about each grid's own mean and pooled over positions or deals, heads and queries.\n- SET: every saved one-layer join of connected/results8 (7 files x 2 rates x 3 seeds = 42 fits), score\n  A(q, j, k) = sum_c Q(q)_c K1(j)_c K2(k)_c / sqrt(R) as in connected/mechanism.py, on 2,000 random deals of 8 table\n  cards, the card you hold drawn from all 81; and the same join at initialisation (connected/bench2.py init, seeds\n  0 to 2).\n- Chess: each join block of the saved chess models, on the first 512 validation positions of lab/results/c24-diag,\n  over the 64 x 64 grid of squares; the same configurations at initialisation (seeds 0 and 1).",
